0,Apurinã language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apurinã_language,"The low transmission and cultivation of the language result in the risk of endangerment. The endangerment level of Apurinã is currently at level 3 (Facundes 2000: 4), which means that although adults still speak the language, children are no longer being exposed to it.",Apurinã,Maipurean
1,Apurinã - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apurinã,"The Apurinã, also called TheIpurinã, Ipurinãn, Kangite, Popukare (endonym), are an Indigenous people who live near the Purus River in western Brazil [1] and speak Apurinã.",Apurinã,Maipurean
